data: {"type":"data-guide","id":"guide","data":{"slug":"zoom","permalink":"/guides/zoom","guide":{"verdict":{"tier":"review_required","summary":"Create and register a General app in the Zoom App Marketplace. Adding scopes submits a security-review request, while outside-user Marketplace publication also requires app approval.","effort_hours":{"min":2.0,"max":6.0},"calendar":{"min_days":0.0,"max_days":null,"label":"External review timing is not stated"},"calendar_basis":"estimate","confidence":"medium"},"situations":{"questions":[{"id":"audience","text":"Who will connect the app?","options":[{"id":"own_org","label":"Only my Zoom organization or account members"},{"id":"outside_users","label":"Outside users or the public Marketplace"}]},{"id":"agent_action","text":"What must the agent do?","options":[{"id":"read","label":"Read Zoom data"},{"id":"write_send","label":"Write, change, or send through Zoom"}]}],"variants":[{"when":{"audience":"own_org","agent_action":"read"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"An account member can use a beta app, but requested scopes still enter Zoom Security Review.","calendar_label":"Account-member testing is possible; review timing is not stated","notes":["Beta apps cannot be published and are accessible only to members of the developer's Zoom account."]},{"when":{"audience":"own_org","agent_action":"write_send"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"An account member can use a beta app for authorized write or send actions, subject to scope review.","calendar_label":"Account-member testing is possible; review timing is not stated","notes":["Use development credentials while building and testing."]},{"when":{"audience":"outside_users","agent_action":"read"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"Publish the app for outside users; the scope request and Marketplace approval must be completed.","calendar_label":"Marketplace approval timing is not stated","notes":["Use production credentials when publishing."]},{"when":{"audience":"outside_users","agent_action":"write_send"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"Publish the app for outside users with narrowly justified write or send scopes, then complete review.","calendar_label":"Marketplace approval timing is not stated","notes":["Explain why every requested scope is necessary."]}]},"byo_advice":"Composio's managed app may be sufficient for a standard connection, but register your own General app when you need your own Zoom client registration, credentials, scopes, and control. Sign in to the Zoom Developer portal, choose Develop and Build an app, create a General app, configure the Composio callback as the OAuth redirect URL, select and justify scopes, and paste the resulting client ID and client secret into the Composio auth config.","before_you_start":[{"text":"You need a Zoom account and must be its owner, an account admin, or have the Zoom for developers role.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"You have a Zoom account. You are either the Zoom account owner, account admin, or have been assigned the Zoom for developers role.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Decide whether the app will be user-managed or admin-managed because this affects whose data it can access and how it is managed.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"User-managed: Individual users add and manage the app. The app has access to only the user's authorized data.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Keep development and production credentials separate and use the correct credentials when submitting for review.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"It is important that you use the correct app credentials when submitting your app for review.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"limits":[{"what":"PKCE code verifier minimum length","value":43.0,"unit":"characters","scope":"PKCE code verifier","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Create a cryptographically random code_verifier (43–128 characters) and derive the code_challenge using the S256 method.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"PKCE code verifier maximum length","value":128.0,"unit":"characters","scope":"PKCE code verifier","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Create a cryptographically random code_verifier (43–128 characters) and derive the code_challenge using the S256 method.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Existing client secret validity after regeneration","value":30.0,"unit":"days","scope":"Existing client secret after regeneration","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Your current secret will continue to work for 30 days after a new secret is generated.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Server-to-server OAuth access token lifetime","value":1.0,"unit":"hour","scope":"Server-to-Server OAuth access token","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Access tokens expire after one hour. After your access token expires, you can request a new one. Zoom does not require a separate refresh flow.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Loopback redirect rate limit","value":0.0,"unit":"rate limit","scope":"Loopback redirects","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Rate limits. There are no rate limits per loopback.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"General app access token lifetime","value":1.0,"unit":"hour","scope":"General app access token","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Access tokens expire after one hour.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"General app refresh token lifetime","value":90.0,"unit":"days","scope":"General app refresh token","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Refresh tokens expire after 90 days. You should always use the latest refresh token for the next refresh request.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"steps":[{"n":1,"title":"Sign in and create a General app","detail":"Sign in to Zoom with an eligible account, open Developer, select Develop and Build an app, then choose General app and create it.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"On the app creation screen, select General app and click Create.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":2,"title":"Complete the Basic Info fields","detail":"On Basic Info, set the app name, management type, credentials, and OAuth information. Choose user-managed for access limited to each user's authorized data, or admin-managed for account-level administration.","actor":"either","human_reason":null,"irreversible":true,"values":[{"label":"App name","value":"[Your AI agent integration name]"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"On the Basic Info page, add or update information about the app such as the app's name, how the app is managed, app credentials, and OAuth information.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":3,"title":"Register the OAuth redirect URL","detail":"Add Composio's callback as a unique OAuth allow-list entry. Keep Strict Mode enabled so redirects must exactly match a registered URL.","actor":"either","human_reason":null,"irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"OAuth redirect URL","value":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"OAuth allow lists (required): Add any unique URLs that Zoom should allow as valid redirects for your OAuth flows.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":4,"title":"Select and justify the minimum scopes","detail":"Select only the Zoom product and API scopes needed by the agent, and explain why each is necessary. Adding a scope submits a request to Zoom's Security Review team.","actor":"human","human_reason":"submit","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Scope justification","value":"[State the agent workflow and why each selected scope is necessary]"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Select the Zoom product and check the desired scopes, then select Done.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":5,"title":"Collect the app credentials","detail":"Open App Credentials and obtain the client ID and client secret for the intended environment. Use development credentials while building and testing and production credentials when publishing.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Client ID","value":"[Zoom-assigned client ID]"},{"label":"Client secret","value":"[Zoom-issued client secret]"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Use development credentials while you are building and testing your app. Use production credentials once you are ready to publish your app on the Marketplace.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":6,"title":"Configure Composio and submit for approval","detail":"Create a Zoom auth configuration in Composio using the own-app credentials and callback. Use the production client ID for the initial Marketplace publication request, then submit the app for approval.","actor":"human","human_reason":"submit","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Redirect/callback URL","value":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback"},{"label":"Client ID","value":"[Production client ID]"},{"label":"Client secret","value":"[Production client secret]"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Use the Production client ID for the initial request to publish your app.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"review":{"required":"conditional","trigger":"Outside-user or public Marketplace use requires app approval; adding a scope submits a request to Zoom Security Review.","submit":["Configure the app's name, management type, credentials, and OAuth information.","Select only the required product scopes and explain their necessity.","Configure the required OAuth redirect URL and allow list.","Use the production client ID and production credentials for the initial Marketplace publication request."],"reviewer":"Zoom Security Review team and the Zoom Marketplace approval process","wait_official":null,"wait_community":null,"cost":null,"evidence":[{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"When you add a scope, you are actually submitting a request to the Zoom Security Review team to allow your app to access specific Zoom API endpoints.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If the Zoom Security Review team determines the requested scope is not necessary for your app, they may reject the scope request.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Use the Production client ID for the initial request to publish your app.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"When you submit your app for Zoom Marketplace approval.","found_in":"visible","note":null}]},"customer_gates":[{"text":"The customer must approve the app on Zoom's consent screen before Zoom issues an authorization code or token.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"When users add an app, Zoom displays a consent screen. If the user approves, Zoom generates an authorization code or token and redirects them to the specified URL.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"An admin-managed app must be added and managed by account administrators, and its reachable user data depends on its scopes.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Admin-managed: Account admins add and manage the app. Depending on the scope, the app can access and manage the user data of users on their account.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Users must grant the requested permissions before Zoom issues an authorization code.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"After the user authorizes the app, Zoom redirects the user’s browser to the specified `redirect_uri` and includes an authorization code.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"gotchas":[{"text":"The OAuth allow list requires unique redirect URLs, provided as complete URLs or base URLs without paths or query parameters.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"OAuth allow lists (required): Add any unique URLs that Zoom should allow as valid redirects for your OAuth flows.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Strict Mode allows only redirects that exactly match valid OAuth redirect URLs.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Use Strict Mode URL (optional): Allow only the redirects that exactly match the valid OAuth redirect URLs.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"General app access tokens expire after one hour.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Access tokens expire after one hour.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"General app refresh tokens expire after 90 days, and the latest refresh token should be used for the next refresh request.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"Refresh tokens expire after 90 days. You should always use the latest refresh token for the next refresh request.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"After replacing a client secret, the previous secret remains valid for 30 days, so update the app before it expires.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Your current secret will continue to work for 30 days after a new secret is generated.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Simple OAuth apps that are neither PKCE-enabled nor native apps must use HTTPS redirect URIs.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Do not use loopback for simple OAuth apps that are not PKCE-enabled and native apps. These must continue to use HTTPS redirect URIs.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"blockers":[{"symptom":"The app cannot be created or configured.","cause":"The signed-in account is not a Zoom account owner, account admin, or assigned the Zoom for developers role.","fix":"Sign in with an eligible account or ask an administrator to assign the required role.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"You have a Zoom account. You are either the Zoom account owner, account admin, or have been assigned the Zoom for developers role.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"symptom":"A requested scope is rejected or approval is delayed.","cause":"Zoom's Security Review team may determine that a requested scope is unnecessary.","fix":"Remove unnecessary scopes and explain precisely which app functionality requires each remaining scope.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If the Zoom Security Review team determines the requested scope is not necessary for your app, they may reject the scope request.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"symptom":"The OAuth flow does not return successfully to Composio.","cause":"The registered redirect URL is missing, duplicated, or does not exactly match the permitted URL.","fix":"Add the exact Composio callback to the OAuth allow list and verify the redirect entry.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"OAuth allow lists (required): Add any unique URLs that Zoom should allow as valid redirects for your OAuth flows.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"prepared":{"scopes":[{"scope":"Minimum Zoom product scopes for the intended API methods","why":"Request only the permissions required for the agent workflow and justify each one.","review_class":"unknown"}],"privacy_policy_outline":["State the app and developer identity.","Describe the Zoom data accessed and why each selected scope is necessary.","Explain that users grant access through Zoom's consent screen.","Provide support, privacy contact, and data-deletion contact details."],"consent_screen":{"purpose":"Explain that the AI agent accesses only the authorized Zoom data needed for the stated workflow.","data_access":"List the selected Zoom scopes and the categories of data they permit.","user_control":"Explain that users approve access through Zoom.","credentials":"State that Zoom OAuth access is used without exposing the user's Zoom credentials."},"review_text":"The app is a General app registered in the Zoom App Marketplace for access to the minimum Zoom API scopes required by the described AI-agent workflow. It uses the OAuth redirect URL registered for Composio, requests only necessary permissions, and provides scope justifications for Zoom Security Review."},"open_questions":["The exact Zoom developer-console sign-in URL was not verified.","The exact minimum scope names cannot be selected until the required Zoom API methods and data categories are known.","The required privacy-policy fields, Marketplace review criteria, and review duration were not verified from the supplied claims."],"schema_version":"1","slug":"zoom","app_name":"Zoom","guide_type":"generated","last_verified":"2026-10-22","composio":{"toolkit_slug":"zoom","status":"managed","callback_url":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback","callback_note":"Copy the exact redirect URI shown in your Composio auth config; some toolkits still show the legacy https://backend.composio.dev/api/v1/auth-apps/add."},"wall_probe":null,"conflicts":[],"sources":[{"id":"s1","url":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/integrations/create/","title":"Create an OAuth app - Integrations - Zoom Developer Docs","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s2","url":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/build-flow/basic-info/oauth-info/","title":"OAuth Information - Build Flow - Zoom Developer Docs","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s3","url":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/integrations/oauth.md","title":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/integrations/oauth.md","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s4","url":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/integrations/oauth/","title":"OAuth 2.0 - Integrations - Zoom Developer Docs","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s5","url":"https://developers.zoom.us/docs/build-flow/basic-info/app-credentials/","title":"App Credentials - Build Flow - Zoom Developer Docs","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"}],"verification_summary":{"total":32,"tested":0,"docs_verified":32,"docs_hidden":0,"community":0,"uncertain":0}}}}

